Step 0 points toward a viable Track B—not Track A. The paper’s central result is an explicit FPT bounded-search-tree algorithm (Theorems 3.1–3.3), so hiding that algorithm would be dishonest; however, its stated cost grows as \(O(r^{rk}k^{(r+1)k}n^{cr})\), leaving room for a compact structural route against a mechanically enormous native graph search. I’m now checking the local harness and existing module conventions before fixing the construction.
