codex
The Track B construction passes all local gates after audit. Its measured gap is now concrete: the standard compatibility-table algorithm solves 8/8, averaging 7,168 set-pair comparisons and about 204,528 exact membership probes, while the spanning-sheet route is bounded at 279 comparisons. The five cheap/in-context attacks are 0/8, and the constrained random prior produced 0 hits in 200,000 samples. I’ve also fixed a relabelling/cache issue so G8 now verifies all 20 transported witnesses and all 20 unrelated keys remain distinct.
