+
+The five failing G6 attacks are minimum element-sum outlier, left-to-right
+greedy, 256 uniform random restarts, equal local option, and local option-zero
+plurality. The first construction version let greedy solve 1/8 seeds; the final
+version forces the first two displayed groups onto distinct sheets while keeping
+them nonadjacent, so connectedness makes that no-backtracking prefix impossible
+to complete.
