diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..ae67aa0686f202a145096e4259b833bdef0bc626
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,225 @@
+# arXiv:1601.03676 — verified weighted-overlap set packing
+
+| profile field | value |
+|---|---|
+| Track | **B — no-tool compression** |
+| Native domain | combinatorics |
+| Object regime | finite discrete |
+| Computational core | CSP/SAT-style packing |
+| Certificate | integer tuple: `n` pairs `[group, option]` |
+| Native objects | bounded set system, nonnegative element weights, `alpha`-Weight overlap, set packing |
+| Intended intuition | decomposition: local zero-conflict matchings are sheets of one graph covering |
+| Domain essentiality | native; no reduction |
+
+This is a native instance family from López-Ortiz and Romero, [*Arbitrary
+Overlap Constraints in Graph Packing Problems*](https://arxiv.org/abs/1601.03676).
+The solver receives the paper's `r`-Set Packing object: a finite collection of
+bounded sets, nonnegative element weights, and an overlap threshold. It must
+choose one candidate from every group so that every pair has shared weight at
+most zero. Checking a witness is just exact set intersection and integer
+addition.
+
+## Trust status and construction
+
+The local generator and verifier gates pass. The required four-vendor oracle
+hardening is **not yet complete**: the bare run and the separate structural-hint
+and placebo runs all stopped before a scored oracle response because the
+configured OpenRouter key returned HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)`.
+The three error-only transcripts are preserved; they are not hardness evidence,
+and this result must not be submitted until the key is replenished and all three
+arms are rerun.
+
+Generation is inverse. A connected regular constraint graph and an independent
+permutation of `q` hidden sheet labels at each group are sampled first. For each
+forbidden option pair on an edge, the builder creates one positive-weight
+element shared by exactly those two sets. All sets also share one zero-weight
+element, and the candidates in a group share a positive-weight group element.
+Every global sheet is therefore a certified packing. The shipped answer is sheet
+zero, known before the sets are assembled; no packing solver is called by
+`make_instance`.
+
+## Why this is Track B
+
+Definition 1 in Section 2 fixes “well-conditioned”: heredity, conflicts only on
+nonempty overlaps with a removable conflicting element, and polynomial-time
+evaluation. Lemma 7 in Section 4.1 proves that the nonnegative `alpha`-Weight
+predicate used here has those properties.
+
+The paper itself also identifies the easy algorithmic regime. Theorems 3.1 and
+3.2 in Section 3.1 give the BST-`alpha` algorithm and the bound
+`O(r^(rk) k^((r+1)k) N^(cr))`; in particular, small packing size `k` is FPT.
+Consequently this family makes no Track A claim. Here the paper's `k` is the
+generator's growing `n`.
+
+The measured exact reference algorithm builds every local compatibility table
+and propagates a component in `O(|E| q^2 r)`. At the provisional hard preset it
+solves 8/8 instances, averaging 7,168 candidate-pair comparisons, 204,528
+positive-element membership probes, 32 component nodes, and 0.0923 seconds in
+CPython. A solver that recognizes the covering decomposition need only follow
+one sheet: at most `(n-1)(q+1) = 279` exact comparisons/assignments. The gap is
+the Track B claim: the mechanical solver is easy for a computer but cannot be
+executed unaided in context, while the compact route fits the no-tool cap.
+
+## Worked demo (`seed=0`)
+
+The smallest preset is hand-solvable: cross out the common element 41, find the
+unique zero-positive-overlap option across successive constraint edges, and
+check cycle consistency. Here is the complete rendered instance:
+
+```text
+Weighted-overlap set packing
+
+There are n=6 candidate groups, numbered 0 through 5.
+Every group has q=3 candidate sets, with options numbered 0 through 2.
+Every candidate is a set of exactly r=6 integer-labelled universe elements.
+The order of elements inside a displayed set has no meaning and elements do not repeat.
+
+Element weights are nonnegative integers.  The single element
+  41
+has weight 0; every other displayed universe element has weight 1.
+For two candidate sets A and B, their overlap weight is the sum of the
+weights of the elements in A intersection B.  They alpha-conflict exactly
+when this overlap weight is greater than the inclusive threshold 0.
+Thus sharing the weight-0 element is allowed, while sharing any positive-
+weight element is forbidden.  All comparisons and sums are exact integers.
+
+Find exactly k=6 distinct candidate sets with no alpha-conflicting pair.
+You must choose exactly one option from every group.  (Candidates in the
+same group share a positive-weight group element, so no valid packing can
+take two of them.)  The listed constraint edges identify group pairs that
+may have an additional positive-weight overlap; all validity is still
+defined by the displayed sets and the alpha rule above.
+
+Constraint edges (undirected group pairs):
+  [[0,2],[0,4],[1,3],[1,5],[2,3],[4,5]]
+
+Candidate sets:
+Group 0:
+  option 0: {8,17,22,27,32,41}
+  option 1: {11,19,23,27,39,41}
+  option 2: {5,6,10,13,27,41}
+Group 1:
+  option 0: {1,12,14,28,41,42}
+  option 1: {12,26,31,34,35,41}
+  option 2: {4,7,12,25,38,41}
+Group 2:
+  option 0: {13,18,29,30,39,41}
+  option 1: {6,24,29,32,36,41}
+  option 2: {9,11,16,22,29,41}
+Group 3:
+  option 0: {4,14,16,24,37,41}
+  option 1: {30,34,36,37,41,42}
+  option 2: {7,9,18,26,37,41}
+Group 4:
+  option 0: {2,3,5,8,33,41}
+  option 1: {3,10,19,20,40,41}
+  option 2: {0,3,17,21,23,41}
+Group 5:
+  option 0: {15,21,25,35,40,41}
+  option 1: {0,15,28,33,38,41}
+  option 2: {1,2,15,20,31,41}
+
+Group IDs and option IDs are 0-indexed.  Return one [group,option] pair
+for every group.  Pair order is irrelevant; group IDs may not repeat.
+Give your final answer inside <answer></answer> tags as one JSON array.
+Example: <answer>[[0,2],[1,0],[2,1]]</answer>
+Output nothing else inside the tags.
+```
+
+The planted answer is
+`[[0,0],[1,1],[2,0],[3,0],[4,1],[5,1]]`.
+`verify(inst, answer)` returns `(True, "ok")`. Dropping its last pair returns
+`(False, "expected exactly 6 group-option pairs, received 5")`.
+
+## Difficulty presets
+
+| preset | `n` | `q` | degree | `r` | rendered chars | answer-space bits | status |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| demo | 6 | 3 | 2 | 6 | 2,244 | 9 | hand example; skipped by hardening |
+| easy | 16 | 5 | 3 | 14 | 7,278 | 37 | oracle run blocked before scoring |
+| medium | 24 | 7 | 5 | 32 | 29,060 | 67 | not reached |
+| hard | 32 | 8 | 7 | 51 | 69,361 | 96 | provisional shipping preset |
+
+Escalation first raises regular-graph degree at fixed witness length, then raises
+`q` only while the 300-operation compact-route cap permits it.
+
+## Gate results
+
+| gate | result |
+|---|---|
+| G1 | 12/12 planted witnesses verify; all answers JSON-round-trip |
+| G2 | empty/drop/duplicate/out-of-range/swap all rejected with 5 distinct reasons |
+| G3 | fenced, tagged model-style response round-trips |
+| G4 | 0/200,000 structure-aware random assignments valid; space is `8^32 = 2^96` |
+| G5 | shipping density 0/200,000; demo exact count 3/729; reference mean 204,527.625 probes and 0.092315 s |
+| G6 | five attacks all 0/8; exact reference algorithm 8/8 |
+| G7 | doubled `n=64` builds, verifies, and expands the space from 96 to 192 bits |
+| G8 | 20/20 composed relabellings preserve the key and carried witness; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
+| G9(c) | 215 chars, 54 estimated tokens, 64 atoms, 279 intended operations — within every cap |
+
+The five failing G6 attacks are minimum element-sum outlier, left-to-right
+greedy, 256 uniform random restarts, equal local option, and local option-zero
+plurality. The first construction version let greedy solve 1/8 seeds; the final
+version forces the first two displayed groups onto distinct sheets while keeping
+them nonadjacent, so connectedness makes that no-backtracking prefix impossible
+to complete.
+
+## Oracle loop and G9 arms
+
+No scored oracle call exists yet. The current error-only bare transcript records:
+
+| arm/preset | model | seed | result | reason |
+|---|---|---:|---|---|
+| bare/easy | x-ai/grok-4.6 | 1610016111 | error | OpenRouter HTTP 403 total key limit |
+| bare/easy | x-ai/grok-4.6 | 947758483 | error | OpenRouter HTTP 403 total key limit |
+| bare/easy | google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview | 206842926 | error | OpenRouter HTTP 403 total key limit |
+| bare/easy | google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview | 1409784744 | error | OpenRouter HTTP 403 total key limit |
+
+| G9 arm | solved/attempts | conclusion |
+|---|---:|---|
+| bare | 0/0 scored | blocked by key quota |
+| structural hint | 0/0 scored (4 API errors) | blocked; no hinted-minus-placebo inference is possible |
+| placebo | 0/0 scored (4 API errors) | blocked by key quota |
+
+The structural hint names only the invariant: compatible pairs over neighboring
+groups are perfect matchings belonging to one common sheet decomposition. It
+does not state a traversal procedure or a derived sheet.
+
+## Use
+
+```python
+from gen_1601_03676 import DIFFICULTY, make_instance, render, parse_answer, verify
+
+inst = make_instance(seed=7, **DIFFICULTY["hard"])
+print(render(inst))
+candidate = parse_answer("<answer>...</answer>")
+print(verify(inst, candidate))
+```
+
+After a valid hardening transcript exists, emit from the repository root with:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/emit.sh 1601.03676 20
+```
+
+## Caveats
+
+- This distribution is algorithmically easy and intentionally claims only
+  Track B. The compatibility/component reference algorithm always solves it.
+- The 0/200,000 guess result concerns the declared uniform prior over assignments
+  that already choose one option per group. It is not a lower bound for informed
+  solvers. The construction has exactly `q` sheet solutions.
+- No external SAT/ILP solver was run. The paper's full generic BST-`alpha`
+  implementation was not reproduced; the exact reference is the natural binary
+  compatibility-table solver for this grouped instance.
+- The canonical key is a strong but incomplete isomorphism invariant: rooted
+  Weisfeiler–Lehman fingerprints plus exact closed-walk traces. It passed all
+  stated relabellings and 20 unrelated seeds, but pathological nonisomorphic
+  collisions are theoretically possible.
+- The 69,361-character hard prompt is within current oracle context windows but
+  may itself contribute to no-tool difficulty. G9's answer/operation caps pass;
+  the missing three-arm diagnostic must determine how much the named
+  decomposition actually helps.
+- Most importantly, the external hardening blocker is unresolved. A replenished
+  `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` and clean bare/hinted/placebo harness runs are required
+  before this family is trustworthy as a shipped benchmark.
