codex
Implemented the native Track B generator using the paper’s `alpha`-Weight set-packing formulation from Lemma 7 and FPT results in Theorems 3.1–3.2 of the [full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/1601.03676v1).

Files:

- [gen_1601_03676.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1601.03676/gen_1601_03676.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1601.03676/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1601.03676/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1601.03676/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1601.03676/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1601.03676/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

All gated local checks pass:

- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000 in a \(2^{96}\) space
- Five attacks: 0/8 each
- Reference algorithm: 8/8, averaging 204,528 probes and 0.0923 seconds
- Answer: 215 characters, 64 atoms
- Compact route: 279 operations
- Canonical-key invariance: 20/20; unrelated distinctness: 20/20

The result is not yet submission-ready because OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded (total limit)” for every bare, hinted, and placebo attempt across multiple vendors. The preserved transcripts are error evidence, not hardness evidence. A replenished `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is required to complete Step 4.
