I found one more contract-level issue in `escalate()`: it could return `"cap_bound"` while the answer was only 215 characters, because it was really capping candidate-set size, not the answer. I’m bounding the family’s declared language explicitly (`n ≤ 128`, `q ≤ 12`) and changing escalation so it exhausts fixed-length degree/option axes before lengthening the witness; `"cap_bound"` will occur only when increasing `n` would exceed 256 answer atoms.
apply patch
