codex
Implemented and locally verified a native Track B generator based on the paper’s weighted-overlap set packing family. The paper’s Theorems 1–2 provide the FPT algorithm, while Lemma 7 establishes that `alpha-Weight` is well-conditioned. [Paper PDF](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1601.03676)

Deliverables:

- [gen_1601_03676.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1601.03676/gen_1601_03676.py:36)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1601.03676/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1601.03676/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1601.03676/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1601.03676/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1601.03676/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All nine gates pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- Five attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference algorithm: 27,616 exact operations, 0.0070 seconds mean.
- Compact invariant route: 64 operations.
- Canonical invariance/certificate transport: 40/40.
- Answer: 215 characters, 64 atoms.
- Additional audit: 920 independent construction and verification checks passed.

The result is not yet shippable: every required oracle request returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded,” producing zero scored attempts and no Step 4 hardness verdict. The error transcripts are retained honestly; rerun the three hardening arms after replenishing `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`.
