\section{Packing Problems with Well-Conditioned Overlap}\label{GenericSection}

We start by developing an FPT-algorithm for the $r$-Set Packing with $\alpha()$-Overlap problem. After that, we provide a solution for $\Pi$-Packing with $\alpha()$-Overlap by reducing it to the set version. Our FPT-algorithm assumes that the function $\alpha()$ is well-conditioned. %Therefore, for the remainder of this section we always assume that $\alpha()$ is well-conditioned, unless specified otherwise.

