\section{Well-Conditioned Overlap Constraints}\label{AlphaConditionSection}

In the next section, we provide several examples of functions that are well-conditioned. That is, they satisfy the conditions in Definition \ref{alphaCondition}. In the first section, we focus on functions concerning the $r$-Set Packing with $\alpha()$-Overlap problem that by our discussion on Section \ref{GraphSection} could be used to restrict the overlap for graph version as well. After that in Section \ref{alphaGraphs}, we provide functions that consider graph properties. 

